   "image": "data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSU...(base64)",
   "n": 1,
   "prompt": "Keep only the hooded wax soldier with the tall dripping wax shield and the long spear, exactly as drawn: the same thick dripping ivory wax hood around a pitch-black hollow face with one small lilac light deep inside, the same dripping wax tower shield with its round brass boss, the same long spear with its brass-fitted head, the same soot-black wrappings and lilac cloth showing through the wax, the same brass-buckled belt, soot-black hands and feet with wax cuffs. The short black wick on top of the hood is bare and unlit, ending in a plain black tip. He stands in a relaxed ready stance with his feet apart, the spear held upright at arm's length with clear space between the spear and his body, the shield held a little out from his side. Three-quarter view from slightly above, the whole figure centred with wide empty margin on every side and clear headroom, the same painted cel style with thick clean dark outlines, flat colours with one shadow tone and one highlight, matte finish, even soft light from the front, plain flat light grey background everywhere else."
